Cross-machine diagnostic (proof A + original code): the ORIGINAL unmodified runner from the source
clone, run on this machine, gives every arm of the package's run exactly (n-CLU 0.8002628; rival@10x-steps
lstm 0.8002628; rival transformer 0.6780552; ...). Against the original run record
(rival@10x-steps lstm 0.6268068, rival transformer 0.4717477, rival@10x-steps mlp 0.6123522) the
gradient-trained baselines differ; the n-CLU, the four controls, the learned blind arms, the lookup
floors and the planner columns are bit-exact. The package is faithful; gradient training does not
reproduce across the two machines.
